<section class="py-5" id="research"><div class="container"><div class="row g-5"><div class="col-lg-8"><span class="text-primary fw-semibold">DOCTORAL RESEARCH</span><h2 class="fw-bold mt-2">Ask a meaningful question. Build a rigorous answer.</h2><p class="text-muted">Doctoral study is an intensive research journey for students ready to investigate a focused topic in depth. Candidates work with supervisors to refine a research question, select appropriate methods, engage with relevant scholarship, and produce a substantial original contribution.</p><p class="text-muted">Progress includes independent research, regular academic discussions, and formal reviews. The exact milestones, registration requirements, and research facilities depend on your field and proposed project; discuss these details with the relevant academic department.</p><h3 class="h4 fw-bold mt-4">The research journey</h3><div class="row g-3 mt-1"><div class="col-md-6"><div class="card h-100 border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body"><span class="badge bg-primary mb-2">01 • Develop</span><h4 class="h6">Shape your proposal</h4><p class="small text-muted mb-0">Define the topic, purpose, research questions, and proposed approach.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="card h-100 border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body"><span class="badge bg-primary mb-2">02 • Review</span><h4 class="h6">Find academic alignment</h4><p class="small text-muted mb-0">Explore relevant expertise and discuss the feasibility of your proposed work.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="card h-100 border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body"><span class="badge bg-primary mb-2">03 • Investigate</span><h4 class="h6">Conduct original research</h4><p class="small text-muted mb-0">Carry out a careful, ethical investigation with regular progress reviews.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="card h-100 border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body"><span class="badge bg-primary mb-2">04 • Communicate</span><h4 class="h6">Present your contribution</h4><p class="small text-muted mb-0">Prepare and defend a thesis or other required doctoral submission.</p></div></div></div></div><h3 class="h4 fw-bold mt-5">Before you apply</h3><ul class="list-group list-group-flush"><li class="list-group-item px-0"><i class="bi bi-check-circle text-primary me-2"></i>Identify a focused research area and explain why it matters.</li><li class="list-group-item px-0"><i class="bi bi-check-circle text-primary me-2"></i>Review academic entry requirements and prepare your transcripts.</li><li class="list-group-item px-0"><i class="bi bi-check-circle text-primary me-2"></i>Prepare a research proposal and any required supporting documents.</li><li class="list-group-item px-0"><i class="bi bi-check-circle text-primary me-2"></i>Ask the department about supervision fit, facilities, and application steps.</li></ul><h3 class="h4 fw-bold mt-5">Applicant questions</h3><div class="accordion" id="phdFaq"><div class="accordion-item"><h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pFaq1">Do I need a supervisor before applying?</button></h2><div id="pFaq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#phdFaq"><div class="accordion-body">Supervision processes vary by department. Contact the academic unit to learn whether you should identify a potential supervisor before submitting your application.</div></div></div><div class="accordion-item"><h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pFaq2">What should my research proposal include?</button></h2><div id="pFaq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#phdFaq"><div class="accordion-body">Guidance is program-specific. A proposal commonly outlines the research question, context, objectives, methods, and the significance of the proposed work.</div></div></div><div class="accordion-item"><h2 class="a